From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: print the build identity at probe

CONFIG_LOCALVERSION is rewritten by the OpenWrt kconfig merge and never
reaches the built kernel, so print the release tag literally and bump it every
time.  Seeing it in dmesg is the reliable proof of which kernel runs.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 13:01:20.217965524 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 13:01:20.217965524 +0800
@@ -2822,6 +2822,13 @@
 	struct airoha_eth *eth;
 	int i, err;
 
+	/* Build identity in the boot log.  CONFIG_LOCALVERSION is rewritten by
+	 * the OpenWrt kconfig merge and never reaches the built kernel, so the
+	 * tag is written literally here and bumped on every release.  Seeing
+	 * it in dmesg proves which kernel is actually running.
+	 */
+	pr_info("AIROHA-BUILD: 5.4.215-rb210\n");
+
 	eth = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*eth), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!eth)
 		return -ENOMEM;
